  "note": "Extended from the four SROIE Task 3 targets (company, date, address, total) to every extractable value on this crumpled thermal receipt. Added the two registration numbers, the invoice reference, both line items with their GST-exclusive unit price / quantity / inclusive amount, the full totals ladder and the GST summary row. Judgement calls: (1) the 'Total Sales Excluding GST' line prints 6.69 on the page while the GST Summary Amount two blocks lower prints 6.89 — a 16x threshold crop shows the middle glyph of the first as a single-loop 6 and of the second as a double-loop 8, so both are recorded verbatim as printed rather than reconciled arithmetically (7.30 - 0.41 = 6.89 suggests the 6.69 line is a POS/print defect, but the page is the ground truth). (2) 'Cashier #' is printed with an empty value and is recorded as null. (3) 'stamp' is the red circular rubber stamp overlaying the GST summary; it reads PAID and is legible on the page but no engine returned it, so it is kept as a model-only value and flagged here.",
